+## v1.3.1-draft amendments — 8 October 2026
+
+1. §5.2 passes XDG and named tool-cache locations to every project child. §5.3 confines only the effective cache paths and preserves credential read denials. §2.9 includes stable effective cache locations in setup identity while excluding run-local `TMPDIR`. This corrects the offline XDG setup failure.
+2. `shaping.boundary_coverage` is an explicitly writable boolean, default false. False or omitted preserves the exact existing Shape prompt; true appends the HC02 public-boundary instruction to primary and fallback Shape only. No deterministic coverage validator or approval refusal is admitted in this amendment; that criterion is reserved for a later policy change.
+
+The amend-1 conformance cases assert offline setup and gate access through nondefault XDG locations, reject an XDG-dropping fake, and pin the OFF and ON prompt hashes. These are draft checks, not a v1.3 release freeze.
